---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const tallies = Array.from({ length: 65 }, (_, index) => index + 1);
---
<Base
  title="The Signals — India Tech Collective"
  description="A sourced view of internet shutdowns in India, with methodology and disagreement kept visible."
  path="/signals/"
  current="signals"
>
  <div class="signals-shell">
    <header class="signals-head wrap-wide">
      <div>
        <p class="signal-kicker">network status / public log</p>
        <h1>The signals.</h1>
        <p>Connectivity can disappear. The record of it should not.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="status-block" aria-label="Signal tracker status">
        <span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p>tracker online</p>
        <small>method: independent records</small>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="tally-section wrap-wide" aria-labelledby="tally-title">
      <div class="tally-copy">
        <p class="signal-kicker">India · calendar year 2025</p>
        <h2 id="tally-title"><strong>65</strong> recorded shutdowns.</h2>
        <p>
          Access Now and the #KeepItOn coalition recorded 65 shutdowns in India in
          2025. Each mark represents one recorded interruption.
        </p>
        <a href="https://www.accessnow.org/internet-shutdowns-2025/" rel="noopener">Open the 2025 report ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tally-wall" aria-hidden="true">
        {tallies.map((tally) => <i style={`--i:${tally}`}></i>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="signal-method wrap-wide">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h2>What counts.</h2>
        <p>
          A deliberate disruption of internet or electronic communications,
          rendering them inaccessible or effectively unusable for a population or
          within a location.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>Whose count.</h2>
        <p>
          Access Now provides the annual global dataset. SFLC.in maintains a
          separate India tracker. Counts can differ because methods and verification
          windows differ.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h2>What is missing.</h2>
        <p>
          District-level event records are not yet shipped in this repository.
          Until they are, the gap remains visible.
        </p>
        <span class="gap-stamp">Gap in record</span>
      </article>
    </section>

    <footer class="signal-sources wrap-wide">
      <p>sources / dated</p>
      <a href="https://www.accessnow.org/internet-shutdowns-2025/" rel="noopener">
        Access Now, 2025 annual report · published 31 Mar 2026
      </a>
      <a href="https://sflc.in/access/" rel="noopener">SFLC.in Internet Shutdowns Tracker</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .signals-shell {
    --signal: #56f47b;
    --signal-dim: rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.64);
    color: #d8ffe0;
    background:
      repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.025) 0 1px, transparent 1px 4px),
      radial-gradient(circle at 82% 8%, rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.09), transparent 28%),
      #090b09;
    min-height: 100vh;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }
  .signals-head {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: end; gap: 2rem;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem) 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.35);
  }
  .signal-kicker { color: var(--signal-dim); font-size: 0.65rem; letter-spacing: 0.13em; text-transform: lowercase; }
  .signals-head h1 { color: #effff2; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 8rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.07em; line-height: 0.9; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .signals-head > div > p:last-child { margin-top: 1.3rem; color: rgba(216, 255, 224, 0.72); }
  .status-block { min-width: 180px; border: 1px solid rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.35); padding: 1rem; font-size: 0.7rem; }
  .status-block p { display: inline; color: var(--signal); }
  .status-block small { display: block; margin-top: 0.45rem; color: rgba(216, 255, 224, 0.48); }
  .pulse { display: inline-block; width: 7px; height: 7px; margin-right: 0.5rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--signal); box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--signal); }
  .tally-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(280px, 0.65fr) 1.35fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.25); }
  .tally-copy h2 { color: #effff2; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.2rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.05; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .tally-copy h2 strong { display: block; color: var(--signal); font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 400; line-height: 0.8; }
  .tally-copy > p:not(.signal-kicker) { max-width: 42ch; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: rgba(216, 255, 224, 0.68); font-family: var(--body); }
  .tally-copy a { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.4rem; color: var(--signal); font-size: 0.68rem; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .tally-wall { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(13, 1fr); gap: clamp(0.7rem, 2vw, 1.4rem); align-content: center; }
  .tally-wall i { display: block; height: clamp(38px, 6vw, 68px); border-left: 3px solid var(--signal); transform: rotate(calc((var(--i) - 33) * 0.035deg)); opacity: calc(0.55 + (var(--i) * 0.006)); box-shadow: -4px 0 12px rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.05); }
  .tally-wall i:nth-child(5n) { transform: rotate(17deg) translateX(-14px); transform-origin: bottom; }
  .signal-method { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.25); border: 1px solid rgba(86, 244, 123, 0.25); margin-top: 4rem; }
  .signal-method article { position: relative; background: #0d120e; padding: 1.5rem; min-height: 280px; }
  .signal-method article > span:first-child { color: var(--signal); font-size: 0.68rem; }
  .signal-method h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; color: #effff2; font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .signal-method p { margin-top: 1rem; color: rgba(216, 255, 224, 0.62); font-family: var(--body); font-size: 1rem; }
  .gap-stamp { position: absolute; left: 1.5rem; bottom: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--signal); color: var(--signal); padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem; font-size: 0.58rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; transform: rotate(-2deg); }
  .signal-sources { display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 0.64rem; color: rgba(216, 255, 224, 0.48); }
  .signal-sources p { color: var(--signal); }
  .signal-sources a { width: fit-content; color: rgba(216, 255, 224, 0.68); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .signals-head, .tally-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; display: grid; }
    .status-block { width: fit-content; }
    .tally-wall { grid-template-columns: repeat(10, 1fr); }
    .signal-method { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
